  "title": "RouteFM and SaveRouter: A Pretrain Once, Route Anywhere Paradigm for LLM Routing",
  "summary": "RouteFM learns to identify and generalize across heterogeneous routing environments to achieve efficient LLM routing, while SaveRouter uses sparse supervision to optimize routing cost and quality. Both frameworks aim to move LLM routing from repeated local fitting toward a reusable, scalable solution.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "RouteFM learns to characterize anonymous candidate models from behavioral context and infer their target-specific capabilities.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SaveRouter selectively acquires informative model feedback and shares capability information across related queries to reduce supervision cost.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "RouteFM outperforms the strongest baseline by 2.23 quality points with only eight observations per candidate on MMR-Bench.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SaveRouter reduces the break-even deployment volume by approximately 1.9–9.5 times compared to the fastest conventional router.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both frameworks address the limitations of existing routing paradigms by combining geometric information with flexible representation access.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
